# Normalize line endings across platforms.
#
# Store LF in the repository and check out LF in every working tree, even on
# Windows (where core.autocrlf=true would otherwise produce CRLF). Git still
# auto-detects binary files and leaves them untouched.
#
# Why: Prettier is configured endOfLine:lf and the `frontend-checks` CI gate
# runs `prettier --check src/` on Linux (LF). Without this, a Windows checkout
# gets CRLF working-tree files, which makes a local `prettier --check` report
# hundreds of false positives and lets CRLF slip into commits, turning PRs red.
# Forcing LF keeps local checks consistent with CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Existing: keep large generated bundle out of diffs.
frontend/prebuilt/** -diff
